4. CORE ARCHITECTURAL COMPONENTS

The architecture is divided into specialized systems with explicit responsibilities and communication contracts.

4.1 XSUS AI Core

XSUS AI Core is the central request-processing and orchestration system.

Its responsibility is to coordinate incoming requests, context, memory, language processing, knowledge retrieval, model execution, response generation, and quality evaluation.

Principal responsibilities:

- Request validation.
- Request classification.
- Context management.
- Language routing.
- Knowledge retrieval coordination.
- Model orchestration.
- Memory coordination.
- Response generation.
- Response quality evaluation.
- Error handling.
- Execution metadata.
- API communication.

XSUS AI Core must remain independent of the repository's demonstration application and must not require the "main" branch's demo project to function.

It must expose stable contracts that allow other systems to communicate with it.

4.2 XSUS Language

