10. SECURITY AND RELIABILITY

Security and reliability are foundational requirements.

10.1 Authentication

The ecosystem must provide a consistent authentication architecture.

10.2 Authorization

Access must be controlled according to user roles, permissions, and service identities.

10.3 Secure Communication

Internal and external communication must use appropriate secure transport and authentication mechanisms.

10.4 Secrets Management

API keys, tokens, credentials, and private configuration must never be stored in public source code.

10.5 Input Validation

All public APIs and service boundaries must validate incoming data.

10.6 Output Validation

Generated outputs must be checked according to their intended use.

10.7 Isolation

Product engines and execution environments must be isolated according to risk.

In particular, generated code and user-supplied projects must not receive unrestricted access to the host system.

10.8 Backup and Recovery

Critical data and configuration must have tested backup and recovery procedures.

10.9 Reliability Testing

The project should include:

- Unit tests.
- Integration tests.
- Contract tests.
- Regression tests.
- Failure recovery tests.
- Concurrency tests.
- Security tests.
- Performance tests.

10.10 Incident Management

Critical incidents must be recorded, investigated, resolved, and reviewed.

